WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Speaker 1: Well, last week it was Lindsey Graham&nbsp;
who was told you are going to have to respond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:10.000
to the subpoena and testify in the Georgia probe&nbsp;
of the election fraud attempt by Donald Trump in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.640
2020. And now Donald Trump's former lawyer, Rudy&nbsp;
Giuliani, has been told the exact same thing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:21.440
Associated Press is now reporting Giuliani ordered&nbsp;
to testify in Georgia 2020 election probe. This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:26.880
not the news that Rudy Giuliani wanted. Now, a&nbsp;
few important things to mention here. First and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.240
foremost, as a reminder, this is the probe&nbsp;
in Georgia. There is a grand jury. This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:40.080
separate from the January six committee. They are&nbsp;
looking into Trump and associates attempt to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.960
Georgia's electoral votes from Joe Biden even&nbsp;
though Joe Biden. This includes Trump calling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.560
and saying, I need 11,000 votes. Gimme a break. It&nbsp;
includes Lindsey Graham calling and saying, well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:56.160
can't we look into what could be done now?&nbsp;
As of right now, the last we heard, Lindsey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:02.080
Graham and Rudy Giuliani received subpoenas.&nbsp;
But they are not targets. They are considered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:09.280
witnesses. The way Rudy operates, he could make&nbsp;
himself a target by showing up and unknowingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.520
implicating himself and others. That wouldn't&nbsp;
come as a huge shock. But at least for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:19.280
Lindsey Graham's attempt to get out of testifying&nbsp;
has been shut down by a judge. And Rudy's as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:25.200
The AP says a judge in New York has ordered Rudy&nbsp;
Giuliani to appear next month before a special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.080
grand jury in Atlanta investigating whether former&nbsp;
President Trump and others illegally tried to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:35.120
interfere in the 2020 election in Georgia. New&nbsp;
York Supreme Court Justice Thomas Farber issued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.840
an order directing Giuliani to appear before&nbsp;
the special grand jury August 9th and any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.640
other dates ordered by the court. Giuliani's&nbsp;
lawyer did not immediately return a call.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:49.680
Fulton County District Attorney Fanny Willis&nbsp;
began her investigation early last year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:54.080
Earlier this month, she filed petitions to&nbsp;
compel seven Trump associates, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.880
Giuliani and Lindsey Graham, to testify because&nbsp;
they don't live in Georgia. She used a process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:03.440
that involves getting a judge in a state where&nbsp;
they live to order them to appear. Now, here's an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:09.520
interesting detail. Giuliani had been summoned to&nbsp;
appear in court in New York on July 13 to present&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:14.320
any reason why a subpoena should not be issued&nbsp;
for him to testify in Atlanta. But he failed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:19.120
to show up for that hearing. In a court filing&nbsp;
Wednesday, Willis informed the judge overseeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:23.120
the grand jury. Giuliani had been served with&nbsp;
the final order instructing him to appear.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:27.840
It's possible Giuliani could file a motion with&nbsp;
the court in Atlanta to try to avoid testifying.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:34.480
Others have already filed challenges to try to get&nbsp;
out of that. This is actually the second time that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.840
the same Manhattan judge ordered Rudy Giuliani to&nbsp;
testify in the Georgia grand jury. He was given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.960
a date previously to appear and he didn't go. And&nbsp;
now he's being told again to go on August 9th. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:52.800
if you said to me, David, you've got a bet, sir.&nbsp;
No odds, just straight up. Do you bet that Graham&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:58.880
and Giuliani testify or do you bet that they&nbsp;
don't? I don't know which bet I take right now. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:07.280
feels very 5050. If you were me, if you or I were&nbsp;
refusing to testify, refusing to appear before a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:12.400
grand jury, after being subpoenaed, especially&nbsp;
when a judge writes, you've got to be there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:20.560
we'd be in a jail cell awaiting trial on contempt&nbsp;
charges, I presume. But here we're talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:27.840
Lindsey Graham. Here we're talking about Rudy&nbsp;
Giuliani and. What's going to happen? I really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:33.280
don't know. The relationship between this&nbsp;
investigation and the January six committee.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:38.560
It involves a lot of the same people, but&nbsp;
these are two separate investigations. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:43.840
I continue to believe that if there will&nbsp;
be charges levied against Donald Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.920
they will come out of the Georgia&nbsp;
probe, not out of the January six&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.480
committee. But I would love it for&nbsp;
charges to come out of all of them.

